deep.reconstruction:
There is no mathematics on this page and nothing to reconstruct. Folio 58v is not a Riemann manuscript page. It is page 4 of a printed lecture catalogue (Verzeichnis der Vorlesungen) of the Friedrich-Wilhelms-Universität Berlin. The page belongs to the faculty of medicine ('Heilkunde').

It is a two-column list of course announcements. Each gives the lecturer, the days, the hours, and whether the course is public, private, privatissime or free (öffentlich / privatim / privatissime / unentgeltlich). Courses listed include:
- Kranichfeld on fermented liquors and on public health;
- Reich on pragmatic medicine and on special pathology;
- Eck on semiotics, general therapy and contagious diseases;
- Ebert on auscultation and percussion and on children's diseases;
- Ideler on dietetics;
- general and special pathology by Hecker, Simon, Horn, Romberg and Dann;
- Schultz on homeopathy and allopathy;
- Horn on mental illness;
- Lauer on syphilitic diseases;
- surgery by Jüngken, Dieffenbach, Ascherson, Gräfe and Troschel;
- Böhm on surgical diagnostics and operative surgery;
- Angelstein and Gräfe on ophthalmology, and Gräfe on otology.

The neighbouring pages continue the same catalogue: law ending and medicine beginning on p. 3, clinics and philosophy on p. 5.

On dating:
- The latest dated publication cited nearby is Kranichfeld 1841 (next page), with Heffter 1844 on the previous page.
- Brücke still appears as 'Dr.' (Privatdozent), and Schönlein, Dieffenbach and Romberg are teaching.
- This fits a semester around 1845–1848. That overlaps Riemann's study in Berlin (1847–1849), so he may have kept or reused this printed sheet; for example, its blank margins may have served as scrap paper elsewhere in the bundle.

No handwriting by Riemann is visible on this page.
